From 701f60255cd46f523cbdb42c8ec9b7d82e9734ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 14:12:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0109 -- SB16 path requires a VALID 16-bit DMA
 channel (5/6/7)

g2k Vibra16 FROZE at "Loading" (iter opl3ec PLAY2). The SDL/0106 decision
banner shows the cause: "is_sb16=1 force_8bit=0 dsp_ver=4 highdma=0 ->
16-bit-high-DMA path", then OpenDevice programmed a 16-bit autoinit DMA on
dma_ch=0 and the SB16 init hung.

Root cause (a real latent bug in the SDL/0106 guard, not just a bad config):
  soundblaster_is_sb16 = !force_8bit && version>=4 && (highdma_channel >= 0)
A Sound Blaster 16-bit (high) DMA channel is PHYSICALLY only 5/6/7 (the
word-wide 8237 controller #2). The (>= 0) test ALSO accepts 0..4, so a
DSP-4.x card whose effective BLASTER carried a bogus/zero H (here: a stale
CFG-authoritative BLASTER with no real H that defaulted the field to 0, which
overrode the Vibra's true H5) latched is_sb16=true and armed a 16-bit transfer
on channel 0 -- an 8-bit, byte-wide controller-#1 channel. The chip never
raises IRQ-5 for a 16-bit transfer on an 8-bit channel, so the autoinit DMA
never advances and every backend (Organya/OPL3/WaveBlaster all ride the
DMA-IRQ pump) hangs silent at init. The hang is latent for ANY no-/bad-H
DSP-4.x config, not specific to g2k.

Why DOS needs this: 16-bit SB DMA cannot run on channels 0-4; "high DMA
channel present (>=0)" is the wrong proxy for "usable 16-bit DMA channel."

Fix: require a VALID 16-bit channel -- have_valid_highdma = (highdma in 5..7).
Any other highdma (the -1 absent sentinel, the 0..4 low-DMA channels, or >7)
declines the 16-bit path and falls through to the existing SDL/0106 graceful
8-bit low-DMA D-channel path. We never program 16-bit DMA on a channel that
cannot carry it. "Valid 16-bit DMA available" is now one consistent predicate
(exactly {5,6,7}); everything else means "no usable high DMA."

Sentinel note: the SDL BLASTER parser already leaves highdma_channel = -1 when
there is no H token (consistent). A value of 0 means BLASTER carried an
explicit (invalid) "H0" -- produced upstream when a CFG/SETUP-authoritative
BLASTER with no real H defaults the field to 0. SDL now treats every non-5/6/7
highdma uniformly as "no usable 16-bit DMA," so the SDL-side behavior is
consistent regardless of how the bogus value arrived; fixing the upstream
"H0 default" is an engine/SETUP follow-up. The raw highdma value is kept in the
decision banner so the offending BLASTER H stays visible in the log.

BYTE-IDENTICAL for the shipped Vibra16 + H5 case: highdma=5 is in {5,6,7} so
have_valid_highdma=true; with the hint off and version>=4, is_sb16 stays
exactly as SDL/0106 produced (true) and every downstream is_sb16 consumer takes
the identical 16-bit branch. DOSBox-X (sbtype=sb16, H5) likewise unchanged. The
new term only changes the result for a DSP-4.x card with highdma not in 5/6/7.

Diagnostics: the required SDL/0106 decision banner is unchanged (still emits
is_sb16/force_8bit/dsp_ver/highdma -> path). The graceful-fallback witness is
retagged SDL/0109 and widened: it now fires for highdma not in {5,6,7} (was
"no H at all") and prints the offending highdma value.

Workspace-local patch; not upstreamed (sdl_ai_policy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 7b666b21f..52ac07f20 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ static int soundblaster_dma_channel = -1;
 static int soundblaster_highdma_channel = -1;
 static int soundblaster_version = -1;
 static int soundblaster_version_minor = -1;
-static bool soundblaster_is_sb16 = false; // SDL/0106: false when force-8bit (hint/#define), DSP < 4, or no high (16-bit) DMA channel
+static bool soundblaster_is_sb16 = false; // SDL/0106+0109: false when force-8bit (hint/#define), DSP < 4, or no VALID 16-bit DMA channel (highdma not in 5/6/7)
 static Uint8 soundblaster_silence_value = 0;
 
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050): killswitch state for the
@@ -4418,9 +4418,28 @@ static bool IsSoundBlasterPresent(void)
         const bool force_8bit =
             FORCE_SB_8BIT ||
             (f8_hint && f8_hint[0] == '1' && f8_hint[1] == '\0');
-        const bool have_highdma = (soundblaster_highdma_channel >= 0);
-
-        soundblaster_is_sb16 = !force_8bit && (soundblaster_version >= 4) && have_highdma;
+        /* SDL/0109 FIX: a Sound Blaster 16-bit (high) DMA channel is PHYSICALLY
+           only 5, 6, or 7 (the word-wide 8237 controller #2). The SDL/0106
+           predicate used (highdma_channel >= 0), which ALSO accepted 0..4 -- so
+           a DSP-4.x card whose effective BLASTER carried a bogus/zero H (e.g. an
+           explicit "H0", or a stale CFG-authoritative BLASTER with no real H
+           that defaulted the field to 0) latched is_sb16=true, and OpenDevice
+           then armed a 16-bit autoinit transfer on DMA channel 0 -- an 8-bit,
+           byte-wide controller-#1 channel. On a real Vibra16 (g2k iter opl3ec
+           PLAY2) this WEDGED the SB16 init at "Loading": the chip never raises
+           IRQ-5 for a 16-bit transfer programmed on an 8-bit channel, and every
+           backend (all ride the DMA-IRQ pump) hung silent. Require a VALID
+           16-bit channel; any other highdma (the -1 absent sentinel, the 0..4
+           low-DMA channels, or >7) declines the 16-bit path and falls through to
+           the graceful 8-bit low-DMA path -- we NEVER program 16-bit DMA on a
+           channel that cannot carry it. (We keep the raw highdma value for the
+           decision banner so the offending BLASTER H is visible in the log.)
+           "Valid 16-bit DMA available" is now the single consistent predicate:
+           exactly {5,6,7} qualifies; everything else is "no usable high DMA." */
+        const bool have_valid_highdma =
+            (soundblaster_highdma_channel >= 5 && soundblaster_highdma_channel <= 7);
+
+        soundblaster_is_sb16 = !force_8bit && (soundblaster_version >= 4) && have_valid_highdma;
         soundblaster_silence_value = soundblaster_is_sb16 ? 0x00 : 0x80; // S16LE silence is 0x00, U8 silence is 0x80
 
         /* Unconditional decision banner (mirrors SDL/0073 always-on pattern):
@@ -4435,19 +4454,22 @@ static bool IsSoundBlasterPresent(void)
                          soundblaster_highdma_channel,
                          soundblaster_is_sb16 ? "16-bit-high-DMA" : "8-bit-low-DMA");
 
-        /* Loud witness for the specific PicoGUS-SB shape: DSP claims SB16 but
-           there is no high-DMA channel, so we deliberately downshift to the
-           8-bit D-channel path that the pre-patch code would have hard-errored
-           on. Names the force-8bit hint for the operator. */
-        if ((soundblaster_version >= 4) && !have_highdma && !force_8bit) {
-            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0106 DSP %d.%d reports SB16 but BLASTER "
-                             "has no H (high/16-bit DMA) channel -- GRACEFUL "
-                             "fall back to the 8-bit low-DMA D-channel path "
-                             "(D=%d) instead of erroring; this is the "
-                             "PicoGUS-in-SB-mode / SB2.0-class unblock. Set "
-                             "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT=1 to force "
+        /* Loud witness (SDL/0109 widens the SDL/0106 trigger): a DSP-4.x card
+           that does NOT resolve a VALID 16-bit channel (5/6/7) downshifts to the
+           8-bit D-channel path the pre-0106 code would have hard-errored on and
+           the SDL/0106 (>=0) guard would have HUNG on (highdma 0..4). Names the
+           offending highdma + the force-8bit hint for the operator. */
+        if ((soundblaster_version >= 4) && !have_valid_highdma && !force_8bit) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0109 DSP %d.%d reports SB16 but BLASTER "
+                             "has no VALID 16-bit DMA channel (highdma=%d; valid "
+                             "= 5/6/7) -- GRACEFUL fall back to the 8-bit low-DMA "
+                             "D-channel path (D=%d) instead of programming 16-bit "
+                             "DMA on an 8-bit channel (the g2k ch-0 init hang). "
+                             "PicoGUS-in-SB-mode / SB2.0-class / bogus-H unblock. "
+                             "Set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_SB_FORCE_8BIT=1 to force "
                              "this path on any card.",
                              soundblaster_version, soundblaster_version_minor,
+                             soundblaster_highdma_channel,
                              soundblaster_dma_channel);
         }
     }
